OL,3,GNEWSACommunity 'sad and wounded' by
OL,4,AAncient Market fire
OL,5,
OL,6,FA clean-up is under way after a fire
OL,7,Fwhich destroyed a number of stalls at
OL,8,FKingston's Ancient Market, as well as
OL,9,Fdamaging a number of nearby shops.
OL,11,FThe Metropolitan Police said the cause
OL,12,Fof the fire, which started at the
OL,13,Fsouth-west London market in the early
OL,14,Fhours of Tuesday, was not suspicious.
OL,15,FThe findings from the London Fire
OL,16,FBrigade's investigation are yet to be
OL,17,Fshared.
OL,19,FVince, a barista at Zega Coffee, which
OL,20,Fwas damaged in the fire, told the BBC:
OL,21,F"We are really sad, all the community
OL,22,Fis wounded by this."
OL,23,APub: 07-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
